// No code needed. The three checks when a new circuit "does nothing":
// 1. Is the 3.3V pin actually 3.3V relative to GND?
// 2. Does the module's VCC have voltage relative to GND?
// 3. Continuity range: is each wire really connected end to end?

// Common values cheat sheet (a resistor is like a valve on a pipe: bigger value, less flow)
// 220Ω - 1kΩ : LED current limiting
// 4.7kΩ      : I2C / 1-Wire (DS18B20) pull-up
// 10kΩ       : button pull-up, partner for photoresistor/thermistor dividers
// 1kΩ + 2kΩ  : divide a 5V signal down to 3.3V

// No code needed. Wiring sketch:
//   Power+ ──┬── Motor+ ──┐
//        band│           │
//         [diode]      motor
//     no band│           │
//   MOS drain ──┴── Motor- ──┘

// How to read the code: first two digits are the number, third digit is how many zeros, in pF
// 104 = 10 0000 pF = 0.1μF   (most common)
// 103 = 0.01μF   105 = 1μF   221 = 220pF

